  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For any real number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>, let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> denote the largest integer less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math>&nbsp;be a real-valued function defined on the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> by &nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mtext>if</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>is&#160;odd</mtext></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></mtd><mtd><mtext>if</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>is&#160;even</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>Then, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>10</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos&#960;</mi><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p>",
